# Google Form response exports.
#
# These hold real applicant data — email, student ID, resume link, demographics
# — for every person who applied. There is no redaction step between the sheet
# and this directory, so the only safe rule is that an export never becomes a
# commit. Keep them locally to test the importer against the real shape.
#
# The committed fixture is app/seed/seed_applicants.csv, which is generated by
# app/scripts/generate-seed.mjs and contains nobody: invented names, invented
# @usc.edu addresses, invented Drive ids. That path is deliberately not covered
# by the rules below.
*(Responses)*.csv
*Form Responses*.csv

# Anything CSV dropped at the top level, which is where an export lands when it
# comes straight out of a browser download.
/*.csv

.DS_Store
